<title>JAPAN: Japan July gold imports down 49.98 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan July gold imports down 49.98 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in July were down by 49.98 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Wednesday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    July 96     June 96     July 95</p>
<p> Total	    11.97	  17.45	23.93</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Australia	 3.90	   4.05	 6.39</p>
<p> South Africa    2.94	   1.72	 4.58</p>
<p> Britain	   1.52	   3.62	 3.00</p>
<p> Canada	    0.87	   1.18	 1.72</p>
<p> South Korea     0.80	   2.60	 1.50</p>
<p> Switzerland     0.76	   2.60	 3.91</p>
<p>Gold imports in the first seven months of 1996 totalled 95.55 tonnes against 178.73 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
</text>
